  "method": "Three independent sequential processes per variant, Python 3.14.7, nice 19. Actual append/checkpoint serialization and temporary-file writes; fsync disabled only inside the isolated probe process. 319 codes x 3 venues x 60 seconds, three price cells per second (172260 cells). Cold flush, unchanged flush, and 10 seconds of new trades. 5ms heartbeat records excess scheduling delay. No vendor connections or production data. Journal bytes and parsed checkpoint hashes match per pair.",
  "limits": [
    "Does not simulate the whole production process, frontend compression or vendor bursts.",
    "Does not measure fsync cost or market-hour packet loss; actual durable behavior covered by tests.",
    "Cold preparation fills an encoded string cache bounded by bars/max_cells; added retained memory is included in RSS.",
    "Preparation wall time includes cooperative yields; it is not a continuous event-loop stall.",
    "No forced or naturally triggered upper-generation GC measured during the flush phases; does not establish production gen2 latency."
